35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found the old apron was patched three times. The firms say the clay is tricky. I’m a little worried about the ground slipping.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, the ground is tricky, but the money is trickier. Planted ground costs triple to maintain, and the fund won’t cover the hard surfaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, I see the same patching. But I’m glad to know our volunteers are steady. They bring real care to the grounds.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, triple the cost is alarming. With the roll down to seven, who actually covers the gap? I need to know if we’re relying on casuals.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the clay is a nuisance, but the heat is the killer. Last August, this spot baked several degrees hotter than the streets.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, that sounds scary. But the firms said small work is okay. Maybe we can just be careful and not dig too deep?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, the fund covers planting, not the hard surfaces. That gap is exactly where the budget bleeds out.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, I worry about the gap too. But our volunteers are steady. They care deeply. Perhaps we can lean on their kindness to help bridge the shortfall?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, kindness isn’t a payroll. With only seven staff, we can’t rely on goodwill to cover the structural deficit.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you’re right. But heat stress kills plants faster than budget cuts. If the ground bakes, your seven staff are just watching it die.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. I just want the ground to be safe. If we dig shallow, will the heat still hurt the new plants?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, shallow digging won’t stop the heat. But remember, the fund only pays for planting. If the ground bakes, we pay triple to replace dead plants.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, don’t worry. The volunteers are gentle with the soil. They know how to help the plants rest in the shade.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, shallow digging won’t stop the heat. But remember, the fund only pays for planting. If the ground bakes, we pay triple to replace dead plants.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, shallow digging is a band-aid. The heat is structural. If the ground bakes, your plants die, and the budget bleeds.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. I just want the ground to be safe. If we dig shallow, will the heat still hurt the new plants?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minato, the heat is a fact, but the ledger is a choice. We can’t afford to gamble on the ground.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, the heat is hard, but our volunteers are gentle. They know how to help the plants rest in the shade.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, the heat is structural. With seven staff, we can’t just watch it die. We need a plan that survives the budget and the sun.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the heat is structural. Shallow digging won’t save it. We need a plan that respects the ground’s reality, not just the budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
