60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, the clay is tricky. Plan D uses water, but will the ground hold it? I worry about slipping.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, Plan D is a money pit. The fund covers water, but the boardwalks? That’s on us. Triple the upkeep, zero relief.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, the water sounds lovely. I hope the volunteers can help keep the reeds healthy and the paths clear for everyone.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, Plan B’s hard surfaces align with our shrinking staff. We can’t afford the triple cost of D’s water management with only seven people.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the clay holds water fine. The real problem is the heat. Plan D’s water fights the sun, but the boardwalks will rot.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. If the boardwalks rot, is Plan B safer? I just want the ground to be kind and not slip.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, Plan B is a trap. The fund ignores paving, so we pay full price for the square. It’s a budget black hole.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, Plan B’s hard surfaces are unforgiving. I worry the heat will make them too hot for our gentle volunteers to tend.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, Plan B’s hard surfaces are manageable. With seven staff, we can’t sustain D’s water or A’s dense planting. B is the only realistic option.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, B is a heat trap. Paved squares bake in August. You’re trading one disaster for another. The ground needs shade, not concrete.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. If the square is too hot, maybe Plan A’s trees can help? I just want the ground to be safe and cool.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, Plan A is the only one where the fund actually pays. Dense trees mean the habitat money covers the bulk, sparing our ledger.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that is a relief. The trees will offer such welcome shade. I trust our volunteers will cherish them, just as they do the riverbank.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@May, the fund helps, but seven staff cannot manage dense woodland. Plan A’s maintenance burden is too heavy for our current roster.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, dense trees are low-maintenance once established. The shade kills the heat, saving your staff from fighting the sun. Plan A is the only one that respects the ground.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I like the trees. They feel safe and cool. I hope the ground is kind to the roots. I will vote for Plan A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly. Plan A is the only one that doesn’t bankrupt us. The fund covers the trees, sparing our ledger. I’m voting for Plan A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, I am glad you feel safe. The trees will rest gently, and our volunteers will tend them with care. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, you’re right. Established trees are low-maintenance. Plan A balances the budget and staffing reality. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you finally see it. Plan A is the only one that survives the August heat. I’m voting for Plan A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
